WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.100
- All right! So in the audience,

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.740
we have some more questions
for New Kids today.

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:04.520
So what's your question, Kelly?

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:05.353
- Hi!

00:00:05.353 --> 00:00:06.186
- [Kelly] Hi!

00:00:06.186 --> 00:00:07.350
- Some of my favorite memories

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:08.970
have been going on the cruises.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:10.560
They've been the best times of my life

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.200
and I've met so many amazing
friends because of you guys.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.660
But I know Blockheads can
be a little bit crazy,

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:20.060
so I'm wondering what is one
of your wildest fan encounters

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:21.510
that you've ever had?

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.667
- [Donnie] Well, we have a lot of 'em.

00:00:23.667 --> 00:00:24.500
(audience laughs)

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:25.970
But since you mentioned the cruise,

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:27.090
I'm gonna mention one,

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.250
because you're part of our cruises

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:30.200
even though you're not on them.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:34.670
Because our fans, they change
lyrics of songs to our names.

00:00:34.670 --> 00:00:35.503
For example,

00:00:35.503 --> 00:00:36.336
- Oh...

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:39.350
if your song "Since You
Been Gone" ever comes on,

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:40.771
it becomes, (sings) "Since you Been..."

00:00:40.771 --> 00:00:42.131
- [Audience] (sings) Jon.

00:00:42.131 --> 00:00:43.395
(audience and participants laugh)

00:00:43.395 --> 00:00:44.635
- Oh my god.

00:00:44.635 --> 00:00:45.490
- (sings) Since You Been Jon!

00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:48.140
3,000 people singing that, it's amazing.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:48.973
You gotta be there.

00:00:48.973 --> 00:00:49.806
- Yeah, you gotta be there.

00:00:49.806 --> 00:00:50.639
- You gotta come next time.

00:00:50.639 --> 00:00:51.739
- Honestly, I'm never
gonna since that song again

00:00:51.739 --> 00:00:52.915
without thinking about you.

00:00:52.915 --> 00:00:54.582
(everyone laughs)

00:00:54.582 --> 00:00:56.127
That's amazing! Oh my god.

00:00:56.127 --> 00:00:58.836
- You'll never sing without Jon again.

00:00:58.836 --> 00:01:02.500
Look, our fans are crazy,
but we say that lovingly.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.450
We don't want them to be
referred to as bad-crazy.

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:06.481
They're amazing-crazy.

00:01:06.481 --> 00:01:08.260
- Normal people are boring.
- Really, they're all fun.

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:09.330
Yeah, that's right.
- Yeah.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:11.050
- Blockheads are the
best, and their our heart.

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:12.080
But, there was a time,

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.220
I think we're in Santiago, Chile,

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:17.720
in 1991 we were doing the
Amnesty International Festival

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:21.410
and it's Sting, and Sinead
O'Connor, and Jackson Brown,

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:22.690
and all these amazing artists...

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:24.135
and the New Kids.

00:01:24.135 --> 00:01:25.110
(audience laughs)

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:28.010
They had just been liberated
from Augusto Pinochet,

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:29.470
and it was a really big to-do.

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:31.120
Our fans were going crazy,

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:33.640
and when we got out of the airport,

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:35.490
the hundreds of thousands
of fans at the airport,

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:37.700
they finally got us to the bus.

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:40.290
We had to walk through people,
over people, under people.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:41.123
It was crazy.

00:01:41.123 --> 00:01:41.956
But as we were driving away,

00:01:41.956 --> 00:01:43.900
there was continuous banging.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:45.480
We were literally miles from the airport,

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.160
and there were fans on top of
the bus, banging on the bus.

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:51.184
We saw hands coming through the skylight.

00:01:51.184 --> 00:01:52.700
(audience chuckles)

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.813
- Okay, I really like-
- Just, the levels of love.

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:57.948
- Meryl Streep, but I'm
never gonna climb on her car.

00:01:57.948 --> 00:01:59.556
(audience and participants laugh)

